<title>BELGIUM: Sibeka announces shakeup, sees 1996 loss.</title>
<headline>Sibeka announces shakeup, sees 1996 loss.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian industrial diamonds group Sibeka SA said on Wednesday it would book a 400 million Belgian franc provision in 1996 to cover the cost of restructuring its  Diamant Boart diamond tool unit.</p>
<p>&quot;Consequently, the 1996 consolidated net income, group share, of Sibeka will be a loss,&quot; the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>Sibeka, which is 54 percent owned by Belgian non-ferrous metals group Union Miniere, had 1995 group net profit of 594 million Belgian francs.</p>
</text>
